# Bergdb item 001, A-COPY (WPs E2 and E3): a new pointer to a node that is
# neither on the writer's paths nor a pointee of a node of them. Node 5 points
# to 7 and 13, 7 to 15, 13 to 11; T(1) gives 13 a pointer to 15. The paths are
# 0, 3, 5 and 13; 15 is 7's child only. Expected: A-COPY (and TREE) fail.
TRACE 1
CONFIG adopt
TX 0
NEW 0 9 I
NEW 3 8 I
NEW 5 3 I
NEW 7 2 I
NEW 13 2 I
NEW 11 1 I
NEW 15 1 I
ADD 0 0 T 3
ADD 3 0 R 5
ADD 5 0 K 10 7
ADD 5 0 K 20 13
ADD 7 0 K 1 15
ADD 13 0 K 1 11
REC 0 0 0 field
VER 3 I
H 0 R 5
F 5 0
VER 5 I
H 0 K 10 7
H 0 K 20 13
F 7 0
F 13 0
VER 7 I
H 0 K 1 15
F 15 0
VER 13 I
H 0 K 1 11
F 11 0
VER 11 I
VER 15 I
DIRTY
END 0
TX 1
ADD 13 1 K 30 15
REC 1 0 0 field
GD 3 5 13
DIRTY 3 1 5 1 13 1
END 1
DONE 1
